? Why is financial data especially suitable for data mining?
+ It is usually relatively complete, reliable and of high quality
- It is always tiny
- It has no structure
- It is never stored digitally
= That supports systematic analysis.

? Which technique helps identify the critical factors behind loan payment performance?
+ Attribute selection and attribute relevance ranking
- Sequence alignment
- Grid-based clustering
- Logistical packaging
= It also removes irrelevant factors.

? To detect money laundering, it is essential to:
+ Integrate information from multiple databases, then look for unusual patterns
- Use only one small spreadsheet
- Delete transaction histories
- Look only at average balances
= For example, large cash flows at certain periods by certain customer groups.

? Why is retail data growing so quickly?
+ The ease and popularity of e-commerce
- Shops are closing their tills
- Retailers stopped collecting data
- Only cash sales are recorded
= Some firms, like Amazon, have no physical stores at all.

? How can a retailer analyse the effectiveness of a sales campaign?
+ Compare sales and transactions with the promoted items during the campaign vs before or after
- Count the number of employees
- Look only at last year's tax return
- Measure warehouse size
= This is a use of multidimensional analysis.

? Which is a typical dimension of telecommunication data?
+ Calling time, duration, and caller and callee location
- Gene sequence
- Hazelnut supply
- Shelf position
= Multidimensional analysis compares traffic, workload, resource usage and profit.

? Which is one of the three fraud tasks in telecommunications?
+ Detecting attempts to gain fraudulent entry to customer accounts
- Lowering call prices
- Building new towers
- Printing phone books
= The others: find fraudulent users and atypical usage; discover unusual patterns.

? Periodic calls from badly programmed automatic dial-out equipment (like fax machines) are an example of:
+ An unusual pattern that needs special attention
- A normal busy-hour call
- Sequence alignment
- A retail campaign
= Others include busy-hour frustrated call attempts and route congestion.

? Finding usage patterns for services by customer group, month and time of day uses:
+ Multidimensional association and sequential pattern analysis
- k-medoids
- Logistical packaging
- Money laundering detection
= It's used to promote telecom services.

? Biological data mining is an essential part of which field?
+ Bioinformatics
- Telemarketing
- Accounting
- Logistics
= It covers genomics and proteomics.

? BLAST and FASTA are tools for:
+ Aligning and comparing nucleotide or protein sequences
- Clustering supermarket customers
- Detecting telecom fraud
- Building data warehouses for banks
= They must allow gaps and mismatches.

? Why must biological sequence analysis allow gaps and mismatches?
+ To handle insertions, deletions and mutations
- To make the data smaller
- Because DNA has no order
- To speed up the network
= That's how it differs from ordinary sequential pattern mining.

? Genomic and proteomic data sets need semantic integration mainly because they are:
+ Generated at different labs by different methods, so they are distributed and heterogeneous
- Always identical
- Too small to analyse
- Stored only on paper
= Linking research literature to biological entities also matters.
